<html>
<head>
	<title></title>
</head>
<body style="height: auto; min-height: auto;">
<p>Ref No: {{{Case.Case_Number__c}}}<br />
<br />
Hi {{{Case.First_Name__c}}},<br />
<br />
Thank you for contacting Qantas Customer Care regarding your diverted flight from {{{Case.Departure_Airport__c}}} on {{{Case.Email_Departure_Date_Time__c}}}.<br />
<br />
<em><strong>-If technical/weather use:-</strong></em><br />
<br />
<strong>Your safety is our number one priority</strong><br />
<br />
As you may know, poor weather/a mechanical issue/a medical emergency onboard- meant we had to divert the aircraft operating QF{{{Case.Flight_Number__c}}} to -DIVERSION PORT-.<br />
<br />
We understand the impact this unforeseen stop must have had on your arrival time, but when it comes to your safety, we never take any chances.<br />
<br />
<em><strong>-If diversion was due to unruly customer use: -</strong></em><br />
<br />
<strong>Your safety is our number one priority</strong><br />
<br />
As you may know, QF{{{Case.Flight_Number__c}}} had to divert to -DIVERSION PORT- to offload an unruly passenger for -poor/threatening- behaviour towards other customers and crew. &nbsp;<br />
<br />
While we understand the impact this unforeseen stop had on your arrival time, we have a zero-tolerance approach for anti-social behaviour and any actions that could compromise the safety of anyone on our aircraft.<br />
<br />
<em><strong>-If poorly handled by us, add:-</strong></em><br />
<br />
<strong>Our commitment to high standards</strong><br />
<br />
We know the importance of great communication in situations like this, so I’m sorry to hear our airport team did not manage this delay as well as expected.<br />
<br />
I want to assure you that we’re committed to improving our delay handling processes when unforeseen issues happen.<br />
<br />
<em><strong>-If offering goodwill gesture to Frequent Flyer:-</strong></em><br />
<br />
As a gesture of goodwill, I’ve credited {{{Case.Recovery_Quantity__c}}} Qantas Points to your Frequent Flyer account.<br />
<br />
<br />
<em><strong>-If not a Frequent Flyer: -</strong></em></p>

<p>As a gesture of goodwill, I’d like to arrange a credit of {{{Case.Recovery_Quantity__c}}} Qantas Points to you.<br />
<br />
Please can you let me know your Frequent Flyer number by replying to this email so I can credit points to your account. If you’re not already a member you can use this&nbsp;<a href="https://www.qantas.com/en-au/frequent-flyer/join/code/familyfree">link</a>&nbsp;to join free of charge.<br />
<br />
<br />
<em><strong>-If requesting compensation add:-</strong></em><br />
<br />
<strong>We’re here to help</strong><br />
<br />
Although we’re unable to offer compensation, you may still be able to claim any unexpected costs through your personal travel insurance. I’d be happy to provide you with all the information you need to make a claim.<br />
<br />
Customer feedback plays an important role in our continuous improvement process so that we can provide you with exceptional service from start to finish.<br />
&nbsp;<br />
Thank you for taking the time to tell us about your experience and hope we can welcome you onboard again soon.</p>
</body>
</html>